1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR HUGH HALCRO===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Hugh Halcro here treated cannot be identified with certainty.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to the late Roland William Saint-Clair's report of the Nobles of Sweden, Sir Hugh Halcro here treated is the father of Barbe Halcro. His daughter is said to have married William Sinclair, Master of Seba and Brobster. 
2 CONC [https://archive.org/stream/saintclairsofisl00sain#page/317/mode/1up The Saint-Clairs of the Isles, p. 317] A date of death has not been identified for Barbe Halcro, although it is supposed that she must have died before 18 Octobe
2 CONC r 1615, when her husband, William Sinclair of Saba, is noticed with his second wife Jean Gordon. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD106%2f137&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=david+king&ko=p&
2 CONC r=&ro=s&df=1550&dt=1650&di=y NRS., GD106/137] At least five men named Hugh Halcro are noticed in Storer Clouston's Records of the Earldom of Orkney but only two predeceased Barbe. Their names follow:
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Hew-Halcro/6000000037000518824 
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Hugh-Halcro-of-that-Ilk/6000000037006810108 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogical Account===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/stream/publicationsofsc27scot#page/448/mode/1up J. Storer Clouston, Records of the Earldom of Orkney, 1299-1614 (Scottish History Society, Edinburgh, 1914),  pp. 448-51 for Drop-line Pedigree Charts for Halco 
2 CONC of that Ilk and Halcro of Aikers]
