1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===BARBE HALCRO===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Barbe Halcro here treated is not the same person as https://www.geni.com/people/Barbara-Halcro/6000000079427108836?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1529445391303&through=6000000034563895032
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to the late Roland William Saint-Clair's report of the Nobles of Sweden, Barbe Halcro here treated is the daughter of Sir Hugh Halcro.This information was evidently provided by her son, Lietenant Colonel David Sinclai
2 CONC r, when he was admitted to the Swedish College of Nobles in 1655. Roland William Saint-Claire cited entry number 626. [https://archive.org/stream/saintclairsofisl00sain#page/317/mode/1up The Saint-Clairs of the Isles, p. 317]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''When he speaks of the Swedish College of Nobles Roland William Sinclair was probably refering to the House of Nobility, in Swedish [https://www.riddarhuset.se/ the Riddarhuset] a palace and an organisation for the nobles in Swe
2 CONC den, whose objective is to preserve, maintain, and shield a historical heritage.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''If Barbara Halcro here treated was the wife of William Sinclair of Saba, as has been suggested by the late Roland William Saint-Clair's report, then she must have died before 18 October 1615, the date upon which William Sinclai
2 CONC r of Saba and his wife Jean Gordon had a charter for the lands of Cowbister and Smowgrow in the Orkney parish of Orphir.  [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD106%2f137&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=
2 CONC n&tp=n&k=david+king&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1550&dt=1650&di=y NRS., GD106/137]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to the late Roland William Saint-Clair's report of the Nobles of Sweden, Barbe Halcro married William Sinclair, Master of Seba and Brobster. [https://archive.org/stream/saintclairsofisl00sain#page/317/mode/1up The Sai
2 CONC nt-Clairs of the Isles, p. 317] This suggests that she and her husband were married during the lifetime of John Sinclair of Tullhop, her father-in-law, who was alive on 3 November 1593 [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonline
2 CONC catalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD1%2f45%2f15&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+sinclair&ko=a&r=&ro=s&df=1550&dt=1600&di=y NRS: GD1/45/15] but probably died before 18 October 1615. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatal
2 CONC ogue/details.aspx?reference=GD106%2f137&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=david+king&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1550&dt=1650&di=y NRS: GD106/137]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
2 CONT
