1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===WILLIAM SINCLAIR OF SABA (aka WILLIAM SINCLAIR OF TULLOPE)===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Sinclair of Tullope is the son of  https://www.geni.com/people/John-Sinclair-of-Toab/6000000000769973224?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1485214873826&through=6000000000769973234 and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Mary-S
2 CONC tewart/6000000025933611872?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1485215131962&through=6000000000769973234  According to Roland William Saint-Clair, William Sinclair of Tullope is the same person as William Sinclair of Saba. [https://archive.o
2 CONC rg/stream/saintclairsofisl00sain#page/140/mode/1up/search/barbara+halcro The Saint Clairs of the Isles, p. 140]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Charter Witness===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 30 June 1618 William Sinclair of Tolhoip witnessed a charter issued by James Sinclair of Gott. [http://vsnrweb-publications.org.uk/Orkney%20and%20Shetland%20records/Orkney%20and%20Shetland%20Records%20Vol%20III.pdf Orkney an
2 CONC d Shetland Records, iii, Orkney Sasines, 1617-21, p. 71]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 7 July 1620 William Sinclair of Tolhoip witnessed a charter in favour of Hew Halcro, fiar of that Ilk. [http://vsnrweb-publications.org.uk/Orkney%20and%20Shetland%20records/Orkney%20and%20Shetland%20Records%20Vol%20III.pdf O
2 CONC rkney and Shetland Records, iii, Orkney Sasines, 1617-21, pp. 114-15]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Bailie for Alexander Paplay===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 15 March 1620 William Sinclair of Tolhoip, acting as bailie for Alexander Paplay, merchant burgess of Kirkwall, gave sasine of a three merkland in Sands, Deerness, to William Irvine of Grind. [http://vsnrweb-publications.org
2 CONC .uk/Orkney%20and%20Shetland%20records/Orkney%20and%20Shetland%20Records%20Vol%20III.pdf Orkney and Shetland Records, iii, Orkney Sasines, 1617-21, p. 91]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Lands of Saba===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 November 1624: [https://archive.org/stream/publicationsofsc27scot#page/96/mode/1up Records of the Earldom of Orkney, note on p. 96]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/stream/publicationsofsc27scot#page/454/mode/1up Records of the Earldom of Orkney, pp. 454-55]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Last Will and Testament of James, Lord Eythin===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/scotsinsweden00fisc#page/229/mode/1up Page First]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/scotsinsweden00fisc#page/230/mode/1up Page Second]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/scotsinsweden00fisc#page/231/mode/1up Page Third]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Sinclair of Saba (aka William Sinclair of Tolhoip) died before 23 April 1657.  [https://archive.org/details/calendaroflaing00edin/page/587 Calendar of the Laing Charters: 2502]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===First Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to Roland William Saint-Clair's account of the Sinclair Nobles in Sweden and Alsace, William Sinclair, Master of Seba and Brobster, married: "Barbe, daughter of Sir Hugh Halcro," by whom she had two sons: - John Sincl
2 CONC air and David Sinclair, both of whom are reported to have gone to Sweden in 1641. [https://archive.org/stream/saintclairsofisl00sain#page/317/mode/1up The Saint-Clair;s of the Isles, p. 372]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children of First Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/John-Sinclair/6000000034563507675?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1529262836521&through=6000000000769973234
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/David-Sinclair-av-Finnekumla/6000000004289437678?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1529262959508&through=6000000000769973234
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Second Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Sinclair of Saba married Jean Gordon. She is noticed as his wife on 18 Ocrober 1615.  [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD106%2f137&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=david+king&ko=p&
2 CONC r=&ro=s&df=1550&dt=1650&di=y NRS: GD106/137]'''
2 CONT
