1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===COLONEL JOHN SINCLAIR (aka JOHN WILLIAMSON)===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Colonel John Sinclair is the eldest son of William Sinclair, Master of Seba and Brobster, and his wife Barbe Halcro. According to Roland William Sinclair's account of the Sinclairs in Sweden and Alsace, he went to Sweden in 164
2 CONC 1, where he rose to the rank of Colonel of an infantry regiment. He is reported to have been killed in 1656, during the siege of Thorn in Poland. His issue are said to have established themselves in Germany, where his male descend
2 CONC ants became extinct in the person of his grandson, Louis Sinclair. [https://archive.org/stream/saintclairsofisl00sain#page/318/mode/1up/search/barbara+halcro The Saint-Clairs of the Isles etc., p. 318]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biographical and Genealogical Accounts===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/saintclairsofisl00sain#page/139/mode/1up/search/barbara+halcro The Saint Clairs of the Isles, pp. 139-141 for the Sinclairs of Tohop and Saba]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/scotsinsweden00fisc#page/n10/mode/1up Th. A. Fischer, The Scots in Sweden (Otto Shulze, Edinburgh, 1907),  278 pp. including index]
