1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JEAN GORDON (aka JANET GORDON)===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jean Gordon is the daughter of William Gordon. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD106%2f271&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Saba&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS, GD106/271]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date of death has not been identified for Jean Gordon. Her second husband, William Sinclair of Saba, died before 1657 [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=SC11%2f5%2f1657%2f47&st=1&tc=
2 CONC y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=sabay&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS, SC11/5/1657/47] but she appears to have survived his death and may still have been alive on 17 July 1662. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?
2 CONC reference=GD106%2f271&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Saba&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS, GD106/271]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===First Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jean Gordon married Patrick Irving of Sabay. [https://archive.org/stream/publicationsofsc27scot#page/455/mode/1up Records of the Earldom of Orkney, p. 455]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Second Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jean Gordon married William Sinclair of Tohop, afterwards William Sinclair of Saba. [https://archive.org/stream/saintclairsofisl00sain#page/140/mode/1up The Saint-Clairs of the Isles, p. 140] They were married before 18 October
2 CONC  1615. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD106%2f137&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=david+king&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1550&dt=1650&di=y NRS: GD106/137]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children of First Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/William-Irving-of-Saba/6000000049241562888?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1502775819356&through=6000000000769973244
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children of Second Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Sinclair-of-Saba/6000000049240423906?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1502775983755&through=6000000000769973244
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Edward-Sinclair/6000000064829903877?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1502776007867&through=6000000000769973244
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/James-Sinclair-of-Grottsetter/6000000018907873210?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1502776202995&through=6000000000769973244
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Marie-Sinclair/6000000047960165848?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1502776239764&through=6000000000769973244
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 October 1615: Obligation by Mr Wm. Sinclair of Tullope narrating that whereas James Bishop of Glasgow and afterward Bishop of Orkney did by Charter of Feufarm dated (blank) sett to him and Jeane Gordoun, his spouse, the land
2 CONC s of Cowbister and Smowgrow in parish of Orphir, without reservation of liferent of either of the said two roumes to Marie Stewart, mother of said Wm., nevertheless he obliges himself to submit to arbitration with his mother and D
2 CONC avid King of Worbister, her spouse, anent what right, title or security he should give to them of the said lands [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD106%2f137&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=
2 CONC david+king&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1550&dt=1650&di=y National Records of Scotland, James Brown Craven bequest relating to local and ecclesiastical history on Orkney, reference GD106/137]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 March 1635: Charter by George Bellenden of Midhous whereby, in implement of M/C between him with consent of Adam B., elder of Stanehous, his f., and of Adam B. younger, fiar of Stanehous, his brother, on the one part, and Wi
2 CONC lliam Sinclair of Tolhoip, and Marie S., his daughter, with consent of her said f., and of Jean Gordoun, her m., on the other part, said George grants to said Marie, his future spouse, liferent of his sixpenny land of Midhous and 
2 CONC halfpenny land Bishop's land in Howa lying in Utter Costa, parish of Evie and Sheriffdom of Orkney, together with one penny udal land in Howa, one penny udal land in Brek, and his sixpenny land Bishop's land called Flaw-is lying i
2 CONC n said parish and sheriffdom [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD106%2f167&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=+Bellenden&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, James Brown Crave
2 CONC n bequest relating to local and ecclesiastical history on Orkney, reference GD106/167]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 July 1662: Ratification by Margt. Gordone, sp. to Patk. Spence, merchant in Kirkwall, Barbara Gordone, sp. to Hary Erby, merchant there, and Elspeth Gordone sp. to Wm. Smersone, sergt. in Capt. Hermon's Company, all daughter
2 CONC s to umq. (dated 24 June 1658) Wm. Gordon, of discharge (dated 17 July 1662) of bond (dated 24 June 1658) by David McClellane of Woodwick, as principal, and Robt. Sinclair of Saba as cautioner for payment to Jean Gordon, eldest si
2 CONC ster of said Margaret G., and others and Thos. Wilsone and John Baikie elder, merchants burgesses of Kirkwall, administrators for said Jean G. of 600 merks [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?refere
2 CONC nce=GD106%2f271&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Saba&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, James Brown Craven bequest relating to local and ecclesiastical history on Orkney, reference GD106/271]'''
2 CONT
