1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JAMES SINCLAIR, BARON OF RANDEL===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to Roland Saint-Clair, James Sinclair,  Baron Randel, was one of the sons of John Sinclair of Seba and Brobster. [https://archive.org/stream/saintclairsofisl00sain#page/319/mode/1up The Saint Clairs of the Isles, p. 1
2 CONC 17] '''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogical Accounts===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/saintclairsofisl00sain#page/319/mode/1up/search/barbara+halcro The Saint Clairs of the Isles, pp. 317-20 for the Counts Sinclair of Lambahof]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/saintclairsofisl00sain#page/139/mode/1up/search/barbara+halcro The Saint Clairs of the Isles, pp. 139-141 for the Sinclairs of Tohop and Saba]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/scotsinsweden00fisc#page/n10/mode/1up Th. A. Fischer, The Scots in Sweden (Otto Shulze, Edinburgh, 1907),  278 pp. including index]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://fionamsinclair.co.uk/genealogy/isles/Sweden.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHN SINCLAIR, MASTER OF SEBA AND BROBSTER, who married Marie, daughter of the Lord B....ng.... [Blantyre], and had sons-
2 CONT
2 CONT * HENRY, slain in Denmark
2 CONT * JOHN, of whom immediately
2 CONT * WILLIAM, next of Seba and Brobster, of whom presently
2 CONT * JAMES SINCLAIR, Baron of Randel, of whom hereafter
2 CONT
2 CONT From this John Sinclair of Seba and Brobster all the Swedish families are derived.
