1 NOTE {geni:about_me} <blockquote>'''BEATRIX KING'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''It cannot yet be regarded as certain but it is quite likely, probable even, that Beatrix King here treated is the same person as https://www.geni.com/people/Beatrix-King/6000000079360681972?from_flash=1&fsession_id=
2 CONC 1529245113511&through=6000000026383233783 who was the sister of James, Lord Eythin'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Beatrix King here treated is not mentioned in Sir James Balfour Paul's account of the King Family. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefou02paulgoog#page/n609/mode/1up Sir James Balfour Paul, The Scots Peerage, iii, pp. 588
2 CONC -94] Roland William Saint-Clair suggested that she might have been a daughter of David King of Warbuster and his wife Marie Stewart. [https://archive.org/stream/saintclairsofisl00sain#page/140/mode/1up/search/barbara+halcro The St
2 CONC . Clairs of the Isles, pp. 140-41] The possibility of this being the case is suggested by the fact that her son James is called cousin by James King, son of John King of Warbuster. However, this should not be regarded as certain. 
2 CONC [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD106%2f123&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=James+King&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1650&dt=1700&di=y RS: GD106/123]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Beatrix King died before 10 October 1676, the date upon which a legal action was raised against her widowed husband for intomitting with her goods and gear. [https://archive.org/stream/saintclairsofisl00sain#page/140/mode/1up/s
2 CONC earch/barbara+halcro The St. Clairs of the Isles, pp. 140-41]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Beatrix King married Robert Sinclair of Saba. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD106%2f268&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=beatrix+king&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS: GD106/268]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/James-Sinclair-of-Saba/6000000049240937845?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1478241487007&through=6000000049240937845
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/George-Sinclair/6000000053376182988?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1485425131127&through=6000000049240423906
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Barbara-Sinclair/6000000053375723877?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1485425268717&through=6000000049240423906
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Edward-Sinclair/6000000053371709923?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1485421425961&through=6000000049240423906
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Charles-Sinclair/6000000053371560871?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1485421514379&through=6000000053371560871
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 August 1662: Contract of Alienation between Robert Sinclair of Saba with consent of Beatrix King his spous on the one part and Thos. Wilsone, one of the bailies of Kirkwall, on the other part, of 7 meills malt mailling of th
2 CONC e lands of Grotsetter which are given back in tack to said Robt. and his sp. and are to be held by said Thos. under revern. of £450:8:6d Scots [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD106%2f2
2 CONC 68&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=beatrix+king&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, James Brown Craven bequest relating to local and ecclesiastical history on Orkney, reference GD106/268]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 February 1667: Letter signed Beatrix King addressed to her son James Sinclair, fiar of Saba then at Edinr., regarding his welfare [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD106%2f121&st=1&
2 CONC tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=beatrix+king&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, James Brown Craven bequest relating to local and ecclesiastical history on Orkney, reference GD106/121]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 May 1667: Letter signed Beatrix King addressed to her Loving Sonne desiring him to return home. Dated at Saba 28 May 1667. Postscript signed "W (?) Douglas" addressed to "Loving Husband" supporting the desire of the letter. 
2 CONC [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD106%2f120&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=beatrix+king&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, James Brown Craven bequest relating to local
2 CONC  and ecclesiastical history on Orkney, reference GD106/120]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''16 November 1667: Assignation by James King, son and heir of deceased John King, late of Warbuster, and nephew and administrator of the deceased Lieutenant General James King, Lord Eythen, to James Maule of Melgond, in the coun
2 CONC ty of Angus, of 2 bonds, dated 18 February 1644, by William, Duke of Newcastle, Charles, Viscount Mansfield, Henry, Lord Cavendish, and Sir William Carnaby, kt., to the said Lord Eythen [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlin
2 CONC ecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD31%2f88&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=James+King&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1650&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Fea of Clestrain, Orkney, reference GD31/88]'''
2 CONT
