1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JAMES SINCLAIR OF SABA===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Sinclair of Saba is the son of Robert Sinclair of Saba [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD31%2f88&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=James+King&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1650&dt=1700&di=y NRS: G
2 CONC D31/88] and his wife Beatrix King. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD106%2f121&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=beatrix+king&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS: GD106/121]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Last Will and Testament of James, Lord Eythin===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/scotsinsweden00fisc#page/229/mode/1up First Page]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/scotsinsweden00fisc#page/230/mode/1up Second Page ]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/scotsinsweden00fisc#page/231/mode/1up third Page]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A dare of death has not been identified for James Sinclair of Saba. It appears that he may have been alive in 1668 [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD106%2f123&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp
2 CONC =n&k=James+King&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1650&dt=1700&di=y NRS: GD106/123] but he died before 10 March 1686. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD217%2f759&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=James+Sinclai
2 CONC r&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1700&di=y NRS: GD217/759]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===His Testament Dative===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 February 1667: Letter signed Beatrix King addressed to her son James Sinclair, fiar of Saba then at Edinr., regarding his welfare [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD106%2f121&st=1&
2 CONC tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=beatrix+king&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, James Brown Craven bequest relating to local and ecclesiastical history on Orkney, reference GD106/121]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 May 1667: Letter signed Beatrix King addressed to her Loving Sonne desiring him to return home. Dated at Saba 28 May 1667. Postscript signed "W (?) Douglas" addressed to "Loving Husband" supporting the desire of the letter. 
2 CONC [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD106%2f120&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=beatrix+king&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, James Brown Craven bequest relating to local
2 CONC  and ecclesiastical history on Orkney, reference GD106/120]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''16 November 1667: Assignation by James King, son and heir of deceased John King, late of Warbuster, and nephew and administrator of the deceased Lieutenant General James King, Lord Eythen, to James Maule of Melgond, in the coun
2 CONC ty of Angus, of 2 bonds, dated 18 February 1644, by William, Duke of Newcastle, Charles, Viscount Mansfield, Henry, Lord Cavendish, and Sir William Carnaby, kt., to the said Lord Eythen [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlin
2 CONC ecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD31%2f88&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=James+King&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1650&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Fea of Clestrain, Orkney, reference GD31/88]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[1668]: Letter signed "James King" addressed to "James Sinclair, younger of Seaba, his cousin," regarding appropriation of a "small possession" in Hoy by the latter's father without count and reckoning [http://catalogue.nrscotl
2 CONC and.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD106%2f123&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=James+King&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1650&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, James Brown Craven bequest relating to local and ecclesiastical
2 CONC  history on Orkney, reference GD106/123]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 March 1686: Summons at instance of John Flett, merchant, burgess of Kirkwall, treasurer of St. Magnus kirk there, against Christian Skeine, relict of James Sinclair of Saba, and David Traill, now her spouse, for payment of £
2 CONC 12 scogs for use of best mortcloth at funeral of said James [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD217%2f759&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=James+Sinclair&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1700&di=y Nati
2 CONC onal Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scarth Family of Breckness, Orkney, reference GD217/759]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1692: Submission by James Grahame of Grameshall, proprietor of lands of Saba in parish of St. Androis, and Christian Skene, relict of James Sinclair of Saba, liferentrix of 9d. land of Saba, with consent of David Traill, mercha
2 CONC nt in Kirkwall, now her spouse [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD217%2f400&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=James+Sinclair&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Pap
2 CONC ers of the Scarth Family of Breckness, Orkney, reference GD217/400]'''
2 CONT
