1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===MAGNUS SINCLAIR OF SKAILL (aka MAGNUS SINCLAIR OF TOLLHOPE)===
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Heritable Proprietor of Tohop and Brabister'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Magnus Sinclair of Skaill is not mentioned in the pedigree proposed by [http://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I82208&tree=CC Clan MacFarlane and associated clans genealo
2 CONC gy] Nor is he mentioned in the pedigree proposed by [http://genealogics.org/pedigree.php?personID=I00500378&tree=LEO&display=standard Genealogics]'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Question of Identity===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Magnus Sinclair in Skaill is the son of John Sinclair of Tollope. [https://archive.org/stream/recordsofearldom00clou#page/145/mode/1up Records of the Earldom of Orkney, pp. 146-47] He is noticed as Magnus Sinclar of Tollope on 
2 CONC 2 August 1568, in the witness list of a sasine made in favour of Patrick Ballanden of Stenness [https://archive.org/stream/recordsofearldom00clou#page/287/mode/1up Records of the Earldom of Orkney, pp. 287-88] and, identified as: 
2 CONC "Manis Syncler of Skyll", he witnessed a discharge made by Andrew Yainistane in September 1572. [https://archive.org/stream/recordsofearldom00clou#page/289/mode/1up Ibidem, pp. 289-90]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Magnus Sinclair of Skaill was one of the suitors who served on the Harmansteine Court held at Kirkwall in Orkney on 23 January 1573-74 [https://archive.org/stream/recordsofearldom00clou#page/134/mode/1up Records of the Earldom 
2 CONC of Orkney, p, 134] James Gray and his wife Kathereine Man raised an action against him in the meeting of the Sheriff court which was held there on 31 March 1574 [https://archive.org/stream/recordsofearldom00clou#page/135/mode/1up 
2 CONC Ibidem, pp, 135-36] and the Fraser family raised an action against him anent the six penny land of Swartabreck in Tohope and the three penny land of Havell there on 12 March 1578-79. [https://archive.org/stream/recordsofearldom00c
2 CONC lou#page/144/mode/1up Ibidem, pp, 1445-45] The case was continued and in the action which followed on 5 November 1579 he is identified as Magnus Sinclar in Skaill, sone and air of umquhile Johne Sinclar of Tohope.[https://archive.
2 CONC org/stream/recordsofearldom00clou#page/145/mode/1up Ibidem, pp. 146-47]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 21 August 1584 Robert Stewart, Earl of Orkney and Lord of Shetland, made a gift of the lands which previously belonged to Magnus Sinclair to his cousin Marie Stewart and her husband John Sinclair. As part of a marriage contr
2 CONC act, Magnus was expected to infeft his son John and his new wife Marie in the land but he failed to do so and it was judged to be escheat to Earl Robert on 27 March 1584. [https://archive.org/stream/recordsofearldom00clou#page/304
2 CONC /mode/1up Ibidem, pp. 304-05] This appears to be contradicted by the instrument of resignation printed below, which shows that Magnus resigned his lands into the hands of the Earl on 17 May 1580.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Bailie for Robert, Earl of Orkney===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 July 1591 [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi05scot#page/643/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, 1580-1593, charter 1902 on p. 643]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Magnus Sinclair died in March 1608, probably at Brabister in Hoy. [National Records of Scotland, Orkney and Shetland Testaments, Testament Dative of Magnus Sinclair in Brabister, reference CC17/2/1, page 49] The Earl of Orkney 
2 CONC took the lands of Brabister from Magnus: "for steiling and grippin the king's landis and vithhalding of certane outbreakis" and gave them to his cousin Marie Stewart, Magnus's daughter-in-law. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/n
2 CONC rsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=RH6%2f2742&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=magnus+sinclair&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS: RH6/2742]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===His Testament Dative and Inventory===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The testament dative and the invemtory of Magnus Sinclair was given up by his son John Sinclair, for himself and in name and behalf of his younger siblings, viz: Henry Sinclair, Janet Sinclair, Marion Sinclair, and Elspeth Sinc
2 CONC lair. [National Records of Scotland, Orkney and Shetland Testaments, Testament Dative of Magnus Sinclair in Brabister, reference CC17/2/1, page 49]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000116062553842& Image of Testament]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                    1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 February 1579-80: St. Andrews: Extract decreet from Act Books of Sheriff Court of Orkney called the Wappinsteine, held at the place of the Yairdis in Kirkwall by Lord Robert Stewart, feuar of Orknay and Zetland, in action be
2 CONC tween Magnus Sinclar in Skaill and Henry Frissall etc. whereby said Henry is decerned to cease from troubling said Magnus in his peaceable possession of lands of Tohope [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/detail
2 CONC s.aspx?reference=RH9%2f15%2f23&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=tohope&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers relating to Orkney and Shetland, reference RH9/15/23]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 May 1580: Instrument of Resignation and Sasine under the hand of William Fermoir, notary public narrating that Magnus Sinclair in Skail within the close of the Yairdis in the town of Kirkwall, for fulfilling of the Contract 
2 CONC of Marriage between Johne Sinclair, his eldest son and Marie Stweartt, brother's daughter to Lord Robertt Stewartt feaur of Orknay and Zetland, resigned to said lord, as superior, all his heritable lands as well conquest as pertai
2 CONC ning to him of old heritage, either in Orknay or Zetland whereupon said Lord 'dimittit' same in the hands of said Johne and Marie to be 'bruikit' by them and the survivor of them in conjunct fee, and after their decease to the hei
2 CONC rs gotten between them, whom failing, said Johne's heirs and assignees whomsoever in heritage, for yearly payment to the king and kirk of scatt and teind as use is. And therefore, by virtue of said Lord's precept directed to Johnn
2 CONC e Langskaill and William Aitkin, bailies in that part, said John Langskaill passed to the lands of Tohop lying in Sanct Androis parish, and said William passed to the lands of Brabester within the parish of Deirnes both within the
2 CONC  'Manelnad of Orkney'; and there gave Sasine of said lands to said Johne Sinclair accordingly. Witnesses, Magnus Tailyeour, Magnus Smiyth, Nyniane Smyth, Henre Smyth, Magnus Prence, Magnus Paplay.  [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov
2 CONC .uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=RH6%2f2550&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=magnus+sinclair&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Register House charters, 1st series, reference RH6/2550]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 August 1584: Letter of Gift by Robert, Earl of Orkney and Zetland etc granting to Marie Stuart, his consingnis for love and favour towards her the 5 [penny] and three farthing land in Brabister, 3d land in Havell and 2d land
2 CONC  in Skartabrek, all within the parishes of Sanctandrois-kirk and Deirnes Which fell to him in escheat by reason of a decreet given in his favour against Magnus Sinclair, father to Johne Sinclair, spouse to said Marie, at Air Deirn
2 CONC es, 27th March 1584, for succeding in his father's vyce for steiling and grippin the king's landis and vithhalding of certane outbreakis brokin furth upoun the kingis balk and bigit housis therupon betuixt the kingis land and the 
2 CONC hill and appropriat the samin to thair avin heritage; and which land the earl gave to said Marie for her lifetime without any grassum, land mails or any other kind of duties to be paid, except skat and teind allenarly. Provided th
2 CONC at said Magnus brook the earl's former gift amde to him thereupon. At Kirkwall, 21st August 1584 Witnesses Thomas Robesoun and Robert [blank], the earl's servants, with others divers, William Guid (Signed) Orknay [http://catalogue
2 CONC .nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=RH6%2f2742&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=magnus+sinclair&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Register House charters, 1st series, reference RH6/2742]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 July 1591: Magnus Sinclair of Skaill acts as baillie for Robert Stewart, Earl of Orkney. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi05scot#page/643/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1580-1593, charter num
2 CONC ber 1902 on p. 643]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/saintclairsofisl00sain#page/139/mode/1up/search/barbara+halcro The Saint Clairs of the Isles, pp. 139-141 for the Sinclairs of Tohop and Saba]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/publicationsofsc27scot#page/468/mode/1up Records of the Earldom of Orkney, p. 468 for J. Storer Clouston's drop-line pedigree chart for Sinclair of Warsetter]
2 CONT #  [http://www.fionamsinclair.co.uk/genealogy/isles/Tohop.htm#Second The Sinclairs of Tohop and Saba]
