2 _MARNM King of Warbuster
1 SEX M
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===DAVID KING OF WARBUSTER===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Servant of Patrick, Earl of Orkney===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''David King of Warbuster is the fouth son amd youngest child of James King of Barra and his wife Isabel Gray. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefou02paulgoog#page/n611/mode/1up The Scots Peerage, iii, page 611]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Murder of Alexander Seton of Meldrum, younger===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''David King and his older brother William King of Barra murdered Alexander Seton of Meldrum on 20 August 1590. The Chronicle of Aberdeen records the event thus: "Alexander Setton, yowng Lard of Meldrum, was slayne be William Kyn
2 CONC g of Baracht, and his bruder, David Kyng, and his complesis, at Barache, the xx day of August, 1590 yeris." [https://archive.org/stream/miscellanyofspal02spaluoft#page/65/mode/1up/search/blackburn The Miscellany of the Spalding Cl
2 CONC ub, The Chronicle of Aberdeen, p. 65]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Suit of Court for Hoy===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''David King of Warbuster owed suit of court for the lands he held on the island of Hoy in Orkney, Scotland. He was one of the suitors of court for the island of Hoy in 1617. [https://archive.org/stream/recordsofearldom00clou#pag
2 CONC e/399/mode/1up Records of the Earldon of Orkney, p. 399]''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Bailie of the Bishop of Orkney===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''David King of Warbuster is found acting as bailie for James, Bishop of Orkney, on 24 June 1614, [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi07scot#page/485/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A. D. 1609-1620, chart
2 CONC er number 1333 on pp. 485-6] and again on 4 July 1615. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi08scot#page/43/mode/1up Ibidem, A.D. 1620-1633, charter number 141 on pp. 43-4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Two Penny Land of Grind in Tolhoip===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 28 May 1618 David King of Warbuster and his wife Mary Stewart sold the two penny land of Grind in Tolhip, in St. Andrews parish, to James Baikie, merchant in Kirkwall. Mary Stewart's name is recorded as Marie Stewart in the 
2 CONC body of the original charter but she signed herself Mary Stewart.[http://vsnrweb-publications.org.uk/Orkney%20and%20Shetland%20records/Orkney%20and%20Shetland%20Records%20Vol%20III.pdf Orkney and Shetland Records, iii, Orkney Sasi
2 CONC nes, 1617-21, pp. 24-5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Charter Witness===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 8 September 1619 David King of Warbister witnessed a renunciation issued by Jean Stewart and her husband Hew Halcro of that Ilk. [http://vsnrweb-publications.org.uk/Orkney%20and%20Shetland%20records/Orkney%20and%20Shetland%2
2 CONC 0Records%20Vol%20III.pdf Orkney and Shetland Records, iii, Orkney Sasines, 1617-21, pp. 63-4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sheriff Court of Aberdeenshire===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 28 July 1640 General James King and his father David King of Warbuster raised a legal action against James Duff, sometime in Burnend and then in Kirkhill .[https://archive.org/stream/aberdeenshirerec02aberuoft#page/500/mode/
2 CONC 1up Records of the Sheriff Court of Aberdeenshire, ii, p. 500] On 27 July 1641 Andrew Cruikshank, notary public, raised and action against David King of Warbuster and his son Lieutenant-General James King. [https://archive.org/str
2 CONC eam/aberdeenshirerec02aberuoft#page/501/mode/1up Ibidem, page 501]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''David King of Warbuster married Mary Stewart (aka Marie or Mare Stewart). She was the widow of John Sinclair of Tohop.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''David King of Warbuster and his wife Mary Stewart had at least two sons.They are David King, younger of Warbuster, [Orkney Archives, Kirkwall, reference D23/6/45] and William King. [Orkney Archives, Kirkwall, reference D24/6/2]
2 CONC  Because David King, younger of Warbuster, seems likely to be the eldest son, it is supposed that Mary Stewart was the mother of all the children belonging to David King, elder of Warbuster. Their names follow:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Major-David-King/6000000049276551916?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1494186007227&through=6000000000769973234
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/William-King/6000000053299758858?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1494186132365&through=6000000026383233783
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/John-King-of-Warbuster/6000000049241341875?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1478243403422&through=6000000026383233783
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Lieutenant-General-James-King-1st-Lord-Eythin/6000000026383891932?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1478243487438&through=6000000026383233783
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Beatrix-King/6000000079360681972?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1540643928152&through=6000000049241341875
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the Orkney Archives===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 May 1618: Charter by which David King of Warbuster and his wife Marie Stewart confirm that they have given to James Baikie, merchant in Kirkwall: "all and haill our twa penny land of Grind with howssis, biggings,, partis, pe
2 CONC ndicles, annexis, connexis and pertininentis belonging thairto, togidder with the towmell or quoyes of Grind adjacent thairto lyand in Tolhope within Sanctandrois parochin, Mayneland and Schirefdome of Orknay". The charter was iss
2 CONC ued at Warbuster in Hoy on 28 May 1618 and it was witnessed by: "Mr. Andro Dischingtoun, minister at Hoy, William King o[u]r Lawfull sone, and Johne Baikie, brother german to the said James Baikie, with certain utheris".The charte
2 CONC r was signed by the following: "David King" "Mary Stewart" "A Dischingtoune" "Johne Baikie and "William King". [Orkney Archives, Kirkwall, reference D24/6/2]
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1623: Disposition by which David King of Warbuster and his spouse Marie Stewart confirm that they have given the lands of Newbister in Sanday to Catherine Sandison. [Orkney Archives, Kirkwall, reference D34/D/1/1/4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''16 October 1629: Sasine in favour of "David King, yor of Warbuster" lawfull son of David King, elder of Warbuster, and his wife Marie Stewart. The sasine follows from a charter by which David King, elder of Warbuster confirms t
2 CONC hat he has given the "nine penny land of Warbuster beneth the hill" to his son David. [Orkney Archives, Kirkwall, reference D23/6/45]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 March 1611: Act of the lords of session in action at instance of Mr James King, writer in Edinburgh, assignee of David King, servitor to Patrick, Earl of Orkney, against Frances Mudie in Brecknes (and) Robert Mudie, his brot
2 CONC her Andro Murray, servitor of said Frances, Gilbert Bannatyne, apparent of Gairsay, John Bannatyne, his servitor, John Skartame and 30 others for spulyie. [Register of Acts and Decreets, 1st Series, reference CS7/262 f.73v-74r]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 June 1614: David King of Warbuster acted as bailie for James, Bishop of Orkney. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi07scot#page/485/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A. D. 1609-1620, charter number 133
2 CONC 3 on pp. 485-6]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 July 1615: David King of Warbuster acted as bailie for James, Bishop of Orkney. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi08scot#page/43/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A. D. 1620-1633, charter number 141 o
2 CONC n pp. 43-4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 October 1615: Obligation by Mr Wm. Sinclair of Tullope narrating that whereas James Bishop of Glasgow and afterward Bishop of Orkney did by Charter of Feufarm dated (blank) sett to him and Jeane Gordoun, his spouse the lands
2 CONC  of Cowbister and Smowgrow in parish of Orphir, without reservation of liferent of either of the said two roumes to Marie Stewart mother of said Wm, nevertheless he obliges himself to submit to arbitration with his mother and Davi
2 CONC d King of Worbister her spouse anent what right, title or security he should give to them of the said lands [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD106%2f137&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=david
2 CONC +king&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1550&dt=1650&di=y National Records of Scotland, James Brown Craven bequest relating to local and ecclesiastical history on Orkney, reference GD106/137]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 May 1616: Discharge by David King and Marie Stewart, his spouse, in favour of Wm. Sinclair, son of said Marie of 10 meills malt and £3:6:8d in respect of assignation thereof to Jas. Baikie, merchant in Kirkwall [http://catal
2 CONC ogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD106%2f118&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=david+king&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1550&dt=1650&di=y National Records of Scotland, James Brown Craven bequest relating to local and ec
2 CONC clesiastical history on Orkney, reference GD106/118]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the Orkney Sasine Register===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 June 1618: At Kirkwall 22 June 1618 is registered a sasine dated 20 June 1618 given by John Diksone in Kirkwall on a charter by David King of Warbuster and Mary Stewart his spouse. The charter confirms that David King of War
2 CONC buster and Mary Stewart his wife have given the two penny land of grind, lying in Tolhoip in St. Andrews parish to James Baikie, merchant in Kirkwall, together with any right they may have there from Patrick, Earl of Orkney and Lo
2 CONC rd of Shetland, and Alexander Loutit.The charter was issued at Warbuster in Hoy on 28 May and the sasine was registered on 22 June 1618. [http://vsnrweb-publications.org.uk/Orkney%20and%20Shetland%20records/Orkney%20and%20Shetland
2 CONC %20Records%20Vol%20III.pdf Diplomatarium Orcadense et Hialtlandense etc., Vol. III.,  Orkney Sasines, 1617-1621 (Viking Society for Northern Research), sasine number 29 on pp. 24-5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 September 1619: David King of Warbuster is noticed in the witness list of a renunciation made by Jean Stewart, daughter of James Stewart of Gramesay, spouse of Hugh Halcro of that Ilk. [http://vsnrweb-publications.org.uk/Orkn
2 CONC ey%20and%20Shetland%20records/Orkney%20and%20Shetland%20Records%20Vol%20III.pdf  Ibidem, sasine number 74 on pp. 63-4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogical Account===
2 CONT
