1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===LIEUTENANT GENERAL JAMES KING, LORD EYTHIN===
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Scottish soldier, who served in the Swedish army, and later supported KIng Charles I, in the Bishops' Wars, and then afterwards in the English Civil War. He was created Lord Eythin after the Civil War broke out in E
2 CONC ngland in 1642'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Without explanation, Wikipedia has rather misleadingly identified [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_King,_1st_Lord_Eythin James King, Lord Eythin] as the first Lord Eythin when he was in fact the only Lord Eythin
2 CONC . He had no sons who might have succeed to his title and, consequently, it died with him'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Birth===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James King, Lord Eythin, is reported to have been born at Warbester on the Orkney island of Hoy in 1589. His father was David King of Warbister. The name of his mother has not been identified. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jam
2 CONC es_King,_1st_Lord_Eythin Wikipedia: James King, Lord Eythin]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sheriff Court of Aberdeenshire===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 28 July 1640 General James King and his father David King of Warbuster raised a legal action against James Duff, sometime in Burnend and then in Kirkhill . [https://archive.org/stream/aberdeenshirerec02aberuoft#page/500/mode
2 CONC /1up Records of the Sheriff Court of Aberdeenshire, ii, p. 500] On 27 July 1641 Andrew Cruikshank, notary public, raised and action against David King of Warbuster and his son Lieutenant-General James King. [https://archive.org/st
2 CONC ream/aberdeenshirerec02aberuoft#page/501/mode/1up Ibidem, page 501]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===His Last Will and Testament===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [http://runeberg.org/ftascotswe/0241.html Will p.1]
2 CONT # [http://runeberg.org/ftascotswe/0242.html Will p,2]
2 CONT # [http://runeberg.org/ftascotswe/0243.html Will p.3]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death and Burial===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James King, Lord Eythin, died in Stockholm on 9 June 1652. He was honoured by the Swedish court with a burial in the Riddarholm Church, on the island of Riddarholmen, near Stockholm, the burial place of the Swedish kings.[https
2 CONC ://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_King,_1st_Lord_Eythin Wikipedia: James King, Lord Eythin]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 August 1635: Power of Factory by General Major James King in favour of Col. Wm. Bailzie, Wm. Sinclair of Saba, his brother, Mr James King, Advocate, and Jas. Lesly, merchant burgess of Edinr., relating to his affairs, and in 
2 CONC particular to the sum of 30,000 merks owing to him by Wm. Dick of Braid, Merchant burgess of Edinr [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD106%2f119&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+king&ko=
2 CONC p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, James Brown Craven bequest relating to local and ecclesiastical history on Orkney, reference GD106/119]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 July 1646: Lord Eythane [Ythan] [Lieutenant-General James King], Aberdeen, to the committee of estates, protesting that he does not deserve their displeasure, and emphasising his loyalty to Scotland. [http://catalogue.nrscot
2 CONC land.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD406%2f1%2f2001&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+king&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Correspondence of the Dukes of Hamilton, 1563-1712, reference GD4
2 CONC 06/1/2001]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''16 November 1667: Assignation by James King, son and heir of deceased John King, late of Warbuster, and nephew and administrator of the deceased Lieutenant General James King, Lord Eythen to James Maule of Melgond, in the count
2 CONC y of Angus, of 2 bonds, dated 18 February 1644, by William, Duke of Newcastle, Charles, Viscount Mansfield, Henry, Lord Cavendish, and Sir William Carnaby, kt., to the said '''Lord Eythen ''' [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nr
2 CONC sonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD31%2f88&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+king&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1650&dt=1750&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Fea of Clestrain, Orkney, reference GD31/88]'''
2 CONT
