1 NOTE {geni:about_me} <blockquote>'''BEATRIX KING'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''It cannot yet be regarded as certain but it seems quite likely, probable even, that Beatrix King here treated is the same person as https://www.geni.com/people/Beatrix-King/6000000049240466839 who was the wife of Ro
2 CONC bert Sinclair of Saba'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Beatrix King here treated is the sister of James, Lord Eythin. It follows, therefore, that she is the daughter of David King of Warbuster. The name of her mother has not been identified. In his last will and testament dated 10 
2 CONC April 1651, her brother, James, Lord Eythin, left an annuity of two hundred Reixdollars to Beatrix and her children: "I ordain my sister Beatrix King and hir cheildring twa hundredth Reixdollars yeirly till hir daughter be provyde
2 CONC d with honest matches and they to have a proportion or tocher good as the condition of the estat will beare."  Unfortunately, the name of her husband, and their children are not identified. [http://runeberg.org/ftascotswe/0242.htm
2 CONC l The Last Will and Testament of James, Lord Eythin]
2 CONT
