1 NOTE {geni:about_me} JOHN SINCLAIR, married to Mary Bruis of Onovitz (Muness), by whom he had a son ANDREW SINCLAIR, who went to Sweden in 1635, and attained the rank of Colonel. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew Sinclair was Governor in Thorn, where he rejected the storm of the enemy eight times successively. He was made Swedish nobleman (Number 965) in 1680, and died in 1689, leaving by his wife, Anna Amendsson, a son, his success
2 CONC or CHARLES ANDREW SINCLAIR
2 CONT
