1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Makel%C3%A9er_nr_513
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lunetta Makeléer (1639-1693)'''  was the daughter of John Hans Makeléer of Sweden who married  Joakim Cronman. (b. 1639, Goteborg, Bohus, Sweden - d. before February 22, 1692/93, February 22, 1692/93)
2 CONT
2 CONT =Birth=
2 CONT Lunetta was the daughter of John Hans Makeléer who was a merchant in Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Siblings=
2 CONT Carl Leonard Makeléer (1633-1663); David Makeléer (c1635-1708) who was the first governor of Älvsborg, Sweden; Catharina Makeléer (1637-1709); Anna Makeléer (1638-1646); Johan Makeleer (1639-1696) who may have been a twin of Lunet
2 CONC ta; Gustaf Adolf Makeléer (1641-1706) who married Sara Carlberg (1647-1701); and Elsa Beata Makeléer (1643-1730).
2 CONT
2 CONT =Marriage=
2 CONT Lunetta married Joakim Cronman (c1635-1703) aka Joachim Cronman. 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT Together they had the following children: Anna Catharina Cronman II (1660-1661); Ursula Cronman (1660-1745) who married Christoffer Fredrik von Grothenhielm (1655-1705); Johan Cronman (1662-1737); Anna Catharina Cronman III (1662-
2 CONC 1685) who married Hans Christoffer von Rohr I (1626-1700) who was killed in action in the Battle of Narva; and Hedvik Elisabeth Cronman (1663-1699) who married Henrik Aminoff (1653-?).
2 CONT
2 CONT =Burial=
2 CONT She was buried on February 22, 1692/93 in Reval, Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Relationship=
2 CONT Lunetta Makeléer (1639-1692) was the ninth great-grandmother of Richard Arthur Norton (1958- ).
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Makeléer
