1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JOHN SINCLAIR OF TOHOPE===
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Spurious Pedigree'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Roland William Saint-Clair was uncertain about the paternity of John Sinclair of Tohope but he listed him second in line after Sir https://www.geni.com/people/William-Sinclair-of-Warsetter/6000000025674858388 and su
2 CONC ggested that he was probably Sir William's son. [https://archive.org/stream/saintclairsofisl00sain#page/139/mode/1up/search/barbara+halcro The Saint Clairs of the Isles, pp. 139-41] There seems hardly any doubt that he made this c
2 CONC onnection because Sir William Sinclair of Warsetter acquired part of the lands of Tohope in about 1514. [https://archive.org/stream/publicationsofsc27scot#page/87/mode/1up Records of the Earldom of Orkney, charter number xxxix on 
2 CONC pp. 87-90] and John Siinclair is afterwards noticed as the owner of part of Tohop.[https://archive.org/stream/publicationsofsc27scot#page/145/mode/1up Ibidem, charter number lxvii on pp. 145-48] Fiona's Finding Service reproduced 
2 CONC Roland William Saint-Clair's account of the family. [http://www.fionamsinclair.co.uk/genealogy/isles/Tohop.htm#Second The Sinclairs of Tohop and Saba] The late Leo van de Plas appears to have followed Roland William Sinclair, in p
2 CONC art at least, but he ignored Saint-Clair's scholarly caution, and went on to identify John Sinclair of Tollap as the son of Sir William Sinclair of Warsetter, and his wife, Lady Helen Gordon. [http://www.genealogics.org/getperson.
2 CONC php?personID=I00546360&tree=LEO Genealogics: John Sinclair of Tollap] Clan MacFarlane makes the same unsubstantiated claim and cites Genealogics as the source of their information [http://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy
2 CONC /TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I82215&tree=CC Clan MacFarlane and associated clans genealogy John Sinclair]'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Question of Identity===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The late Joseph Storer Clouston believed that John Sinclair of Tohop was a close relative of Sir https://www.geni.com/people/William-Sinclair-of-Warsetter/6000000025674858388 but he did not believe that they were father and son
2 CONC . He had this to say about the laird of Tohop: "John Sinclair, first of Tohop, was evidently closely akin to Sir William (cf. nos. xxxix and lxvii), though it is pretty certain he was not his son; for if, as seems likely, it is th
2 CONC e same John who appears in nos. cii, civ, and cv, he was a son of Magnus and Margaret Sinclair (for them see p. 416).” [https://archive.org/stream/publicationsofsc27scot#page/468/mode/1up Records of the Earldom of Orkney, see note
2 CONC  following the drop-line pedigree chart for Sinclair of Warsetter in page 468]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Battle of Summerdale===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Sinclair of Tohope (aka Johne Sinclare of Tollop) was present at the Battle of Summerdale,which took place in Orkney on 19 May 1529. On 19 September 1539 John Sinclair of Tohope and twenty-nine others had a respite from th
2 CONC e crown for their "art and part of the slauchter" of the late John, Earl of Caithness. An abridged transcript of the respite was printed in the Records of the Earldom of Orkney [https://archive.org/stream/publicationsofsc27scot#pa
2 CONC ge/60/mode/1up Records of the Earldom of Orkney, pp. 60-1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Sinclair of Tohope was alive on 19 September 1539 [https://archive.org/stream/recordsofearldom00clou#page/60/mode/1up Records of the Earldom of Orkney, pp. 60-1] but he appears to have been succeeded by his son Mangus Sinc
2 CONC lair of Skaill before 2 August 1568. [https://archive.org/stream/recordsofearldom00clou#page/287/mode/1up Ibidem,  pp. 287-88]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/saintclairsofisl00sain#page/140/mode/1up The Saint Clairs of the Isles, pp. 139-141 for the Sinclairs of Tohop and Saba]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/publicationsofsc27scot#page/468/mode/1up Records of the Earldom of Orkney, p. 468 for J. Storer Clouston's drop-line pedigree chart for Sinclair of Warsetter]
