2 CONT '''James King here treated is the son of John King of Warbuster. The name of his mother is not mentioned in his baptismal record but he seems likely to be the son of Margaret Buchan. His baptismal record is in a poor state of pres
2 CONC ervation but parts of it can still be read: "Jon King of Hoy ane sone baprised call[it] James Witnes James King . . . . ." [National Records of Scotland, Ellon Baptisms, 1640-1739, reference OPR.192/1 p. 19] [https://www.geni.com/
2 CONC documents/view?doc_id=6000000078557490519& Image of Baptismal Record]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date and place of death has not been identified for James King here treated but he seems likely to have died before 19 November 1648, the date upon which the baptism of his younger brother of the same name was registered at E
2 CONC llon in Aberdeenshire, Scotland. [National Records of Scotland, Ellon Baptisms, 1640-1739, reference OPR.192/1 p. 78] [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000078558337843& Image of Baptismal Record]'''
