1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JAMES KING OF WARBUSTER===
2 CONT
2 CONT >'''James King of Warbuster is the son and heir of deceased John King, late of Warbuster, and the nephew and administrator of the deceased Lieutenant General James, Lord Eythen. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalog
2 CONC ue/details.aspx?reference=GD31%2f88&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+king&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1650&dt=1750&di=y NRS: GD31/88] In a letter which may belong to 1668 he identifies himself as the cousin of James Sinclair of Saba, [http://
2 CONC catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD106%2f123&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+king&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS: GD106/123] a fact which suggests that he may be the grandson of Marie Stewart. 
2 CONC [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD106%2f123&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+king&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS: GD106/123] This cannot be regarded as certain, however, for James Sincl
2 CONC air of Saba was the son of Beatrix King. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD106%2f121&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=beatrix+king&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS: GD106/121]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James King of Warbuster was born before 19 November 1648, the date upon which his baptism was registered at Ellon in Aberdeenshire, Scotland. His baptismal record is in a poor state of preservation but the following words can s
2 CONC till be read: "The sd day ane so[ne] la[wful] to Jon King in Dudwick called James befoir witnes Collonell James King James [Gordon] . . . . . Smithe". [National Records of Scotland, Ellon Baptisms, 1640-1739, reference OPR.192/1 p
2 CONC . 78] [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000078558337843& Image of Baptismal Record]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to Sir James Balfour Paul, James King of Warbuster and his brother Henry were in Swedish service. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefou02paulgoog#page/n611/mode/1up Scots Peerage: 611]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Last Will and Testament of James, Lord Eythin===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/scotsinsweden00fisc#page/229/mode/1up First Page]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/scotsinsweden00fisc#page/230/mode/1up Second Page ]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/scotsinsweden00fisc#page/231/mode/1up third Page]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''16 November 1667: Assignation by James King, son and heir of deceased John King, late of Warbuster, and nephew and administrator of the deceased Lieutenant General James King, Lord Eythen to James Maule of Melgond, in the count
2 CONC y of Angus, of 2 bonds, dated 18 February 1644, by William, Duke of Newcastle, Charles, Viscount Mansfield, Henry, Lord Cavendish, and Sir William Carnaby, kt., to the said Lord Eythen  [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlin
2 CONC ecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD31%2f88&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+king&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1650&dt=1750&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Fea of Clestrain, Orkney, reference GD31/88]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 February 1667: Letter signed Beatrix King addressed to her son James Sinclair, fiar of Saba then at Edinr., regarding his welfare [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD106%2f121&st=1&
2 CONC tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=beatrix+king&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, James Brown Craven bequest relating to local and ecclesiastical history on Orkney, reference GD106/121]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[1668]: Letter signed "James King" addressed to "James Sinclair, younger of Seaba, his cousin" regarding appropriation of a "small possession" in Hoy by the latter's father without count and reckoning [http://catalogue.nrscotla
2 CONC nd.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD106%2f123&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+king&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y James Brown Craven bequest relating to local and ecclesiastical history on Orkney, reference GD106/123
2 CONC ]'''
2 CONT
