1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===MARGARET SINCLAIR===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In a Rental dated 3 July 1492, Margaret Sinclair held a tack for a five penny land at Cairston in the Orkney parish of Stromness. It was probably her husband, Magnus Sinclair, who is noticed on the same date holding a tack for 
2 CONC the Bull of Cairston a sixteen penny land. [https://archive.org/stream/recordsofearldom00clou#page/410/mode/1up Records of the Earldom of Orkney, Rental, p. 410]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Question of identity===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret Sinclair is probably that daughter of Alexander Sinclair (aka Thom Sincler) and his wife Margaret Wilson who agreed to transfer all her heritage rights in Orkney and Shetland to her son John Sinclair on 20 May 1527, in
2 CONC  return for his support and maintenance during all the remaining days of her lifetime. [https://archive.org/stream/recordsofearldom00clou#page/208/mode/1up Records of the Earldom of Orkney, CIV on p. 208] Her sister Cristiane Sinc
2 CONC lair sold her rights in Orkney and Shetland to John Sinclair of Tollop on 17 March 1522-23. John Sinclair of Tollop is probably Margaret Sinclair's son. [https://archive.org/stream/recordsofearldom00clou#page/205/mode/1up Ibidem, 
2 CONC  CII on pp. 205-06]'''
1 FAMC @F6000000049695425070@
1 FAMS @F6000000049695622967@
1 RFN geni:6000000049695349104
1 SUBM @S6000000008879398364@
1 CHAN
2 DATE 27 NOV 2020
3 TIME 14:58:12
0 @I6000000049695622963@ INDI
1 NAME Magnus /Sinclair/ Tacksman of Cairston
2 GIVN Magnus
2 SURN Sinclair
2 NSFX Tacksman of Cairston
2 _MARNM Sinclair
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE BEF 15 FEB 1528
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===MAGNUS SINCLAIR===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===[https://archive.org/stream/recordsofearldom00clou#page/410/mode/1up Tacksman of Cairston]===
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Magnus Sinclair here treated is not the same person as https://www.geni.com/people/Magnus-Sinclair-of-Warsetter/6000000042531785778 whose father https://www.geni.com/people/William-Sinclair-of-Warsetter/600000002567
2 CONC 4858388?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1485171008156&through=600000004253178577 purchased parts of  the lands of Tohope from Nicol Fraser (aka Nicoll Fresell) in June 1514.  [https://archive.org/stream/recordsofearldom00clou#page/87/mod
2 CONC e/1up Records of the Earldonm of Orkney, charter number XXXIX on pp. 87-90] Magnus Sinclair here treated died before 24 February 1528 [https://archive.org/stream/recordsofearldom00clou#page/209/mode/1up Records of the Earldom of O
2 CONC rkney, charter number CV on p. 209] whereas https://www.geni.com/people/Magnus-Sinclair-of-Warsetter/6000000042531785778 appears still to have been alive on 19 September 1539.'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Tacksman of Cairston===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 3 July 1492 Magnus Sinclair held a tack for the Bull of Cairston, which was a fifteen penny land. On the same date his wife Margaret Sinclair held a tack for a five penny land there called How. [https://archive.org/stream/re
2 CONC cordsofearldom00clou#page/410/mode/1up Ibidem, p. 410]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Magnus Sinclair died before 24 February 1528, the date upon which Ellen Clouston and her sisters sold their three merklands in the tunship of Clouston to: "Johne Sinclair, son and lawful heir to the deceased Maw Sinclair." [htt
2 CONC ps://archive.org/stream/recordsofearldom00clou#page/209/mode/1up Records of the Earldom of Orkney, charter number CV on p. 209]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Magnus Sinclair married Margaret Sinclair, one of the daughters and heirs of the deceased Alexander Sinclair and his wife Margaret Wilson. She is noticed on 20 May 1528, when she resigned in favour of her son John, her sister p
2 CONC art of the land and heritage which she held in Orkney and Shetland. [https://archive.org/stream/recordsofearldom00clou#page/208/mode/1up Ibidem, charter number CIV on p. 208] Margaret's son John is not noticed with a territorial d
2 CONC esignation but he is probably the same person as John Sinclair of Tollop, who purchsed the rights and heritage of his mother's nephews, William and Henry Paulson, on 17 March 1523. [https://archive.org/stream/recordsofearldom00clo
2 CONC u#page/205/mode/1up Ibidem,  charter number CII on pp. 205-06]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Magnus Sinclair is the father of John Sinclair. [https://archive.org/stream/recordsofearldom00clou#page/209/mode/1up Records of the Earldom of Orkney, p. 209 A link to him follows:]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/John-Sinclair-of-Tollap/6000000025674996034?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1485171780430&through=6000000049695622963 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy Accounts===
2 CONT
