1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ALEXANDER SINCLAIR (aka THOM SINCLER)===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alexander Sinclair is noticed on 3 July 1492, as the tacksman of a seven penny land at Southirqwy and a sixteen penny land at Lerely, both in the Orkney parish of Sandwick. [https://archive.org/stream/recordsofearldom00clou#pag
2 CONC e/408/mode/1up Records of the Earldom of Orkney, p. 408] On the same date he also held a tack for a three penny land in Inner Stromness. [https://archive.org/stream/recordsofearldom00clou#page/410/mode/1up Ibidem, p. 410] and he w
2 CONC as the tacksman of the lands called Stanagar there on 27 April 1503. [https://archive.org/stream/recordsofearldom00clou#page/414/mode/1up Ibidem, p. 414]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alexander Sinclair, identified as Thom Sinclair rather than Alexander Sinclair, died before 17 March 1522-23, the date upon which his daughter Cristiane Sinclair, following the death of her parents, sold all her rights and heir
2 CONC ship in Orkney and Shetland to John Sinclair of Tollop. [https://archive.org/stream/recordsofearldom00clou#page/205/mode/1up Records of the Earldom of Orkney, charter CII on pp. 205-06] On 20 May 1527 his daughter Margaret Sinclai
2 CONC r transferred all her rights in Orkney and Shetland to her son John Sinclair, who is very likely the same person as John Sinclair of Tollop, in return for his support and maintenance during all the remaining days of her life. [htt
2 CONC ps://archive.org/stream/recordsofearldom00clou#page/208/mode/1up Ibidem, charter CIV on p. 208]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alexander Sinclair married Margaret Wilson.  [https://archive.org/stream/recordsofearldom00clou#page/208/mode/1up Ibidem, charter CIV on p. 208] She died before 17 March 1522-23. [https://archive.org/stream/recordsofearldom00cl
2 CONC ou#page/205/mode/1up Records of the Earldom of Orkney, charter CII on pp. 205-06]'''
2 CONT
