1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir Patrick Acheson, Baronet [S 1628] of Market Hill</strong>, son and heir by 1st wife; was (with his father) made a denizen of Ireland, 12 February 1628; succeeded to the Baronetcy, October 1634. He married in 1634 Mart
2 CONC ha, only child of William (not John) Moore, or More, of London, one of the Clerks of the Signet ordinary. He died s.p.m., 6 October, in his 28th year, and was buried 24th at St Martin's in the Fields, Middlesex. His widow died at 
2 CONC St Margaret's, Westminster, and was buried 21 February 1674/5 at St Martin's."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n353/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; Vol. II; page 334-335
