1 NAME Hector /MacLean/ 2nd Baronet, and 18th Clan Chief
2 GIVN Hector
2 SURN MacLean
2 NSFX 2nd Baronet, and 18th Clan Chief
2 _MARNM Maclean
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1620
2 PLAC Scotland
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 20 JUL 1651
2 PLAC Battle of Inverkeithing
2 ADDR
3 CITY Inverkeithing
3 CTRY Scotland
1 OCCU Baronet 2 of Morvaren
1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  
2 CONT
2 CONT Hector was the son of Sir Lachlan Maclean, 1st Baronet and succeeded him at his death in 1649. His mother was Mary MacLeod, the second daughter of Sir Roderick MacLeod. At Hector's death in 1651, he was succeeded as Clan Maclean C
2 CONC hief by his brother, Sir Allan Maclean, 3rd Baronet. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hector was killed fighting for the Royalists at the battle of Inverkeithing. It was during this battle that seven brothers died protecting their Clan chief. Each brother crying "Another for Hector" as they stepped forward to prote
2 CONC ct him. Fear eile airson Eachuinn (from Scottish Gaelic: "Another for Hector") became one of the two slogans used by Clan Maclean. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir Hector Maclean, Baronet [S 1631] of Morven</strong>, 1st son and heir, born about 1625; succeeded to the Baronetcy, 18 April 1649; raised 700 men of his clan for the Royal clause, with whom he was defeated and slain a
2 CONC t the battle of Innerkeithing in 1651. He died unmarried."
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
