2 CONT
2 CONT Georg Gustav von Aderkas
2 CONT Born 3 Jul 1699 in Poenal, Wiek, Estlandmap
2 CONT ANCESTORS ancestors
2 CONT Son of Otto Reinhold von Aderkas and Anna Margaretha von Lieven
2 CONT [sibling(s) unknown]
2 CONT Husband of Helena Christina von Rohr — married 16 Jul 1728 [location unknown]
2 CONT Husband of Margaretha Elisabeth von Pistohlkors — married 23 Sep 1740 in Hannehl, Wiek, Estlandmap
2 CONT DESCENDANTS descendants
2 CONT Father of Reinhold Wilhelm von Aderkas and Gerdruta Elisabeth von Aderkas
2 CONT Died after 1778 after age 78 [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT GEORG GUSTAV VON ADERKAS a. Tackfer und Sallajöggi was * 3 and bap. 7.vii.1699, Ksp. Poenal[1]. He was an Assessor, 1736; Hakenrichter, 1745; and Mannrichter, 1778[2]. He was presumably responsible for the construction of the fine
2 CONC  baroque manor house at Sallajögi (now ruined) in the 1760s[3]. He and his fourth wife commissioned an altarpiece depicting Christ on the cross and the Last Supper for the parish church of Poenal in 1764, which painting has recent
2 CONC ly been restored and was exhibited at the Art Museum of Estonia, 2017-2018[4].
2 CONT
2 CONT He oo (1) Helena Christina von Rohr who + 30.iii.1736, Ksp. Poenal[5]. He oo (2) Baronesse Gerdruta Margaretha von Taube who was bu. 25.iii.1739, Ksp. Poenal[6]. He oo (3) 23.ix.1740, Ksp. Hannehl, to MARGARETHA ELISABETH VON PIST
2 CONC OHLKORS, daughter of Johann Erik von Pistohlkors, who was bap. 2.iv.1722, Ksp. Hannehl[7]. She was bu. 5.xii.1748, Ksp. Poenal[8]. He oo (4) Johanna Helene von Güldenlohd, who was * 15.viii.1706[9].
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
