1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===MAGNUS PAULSON (aka MAWNIS PAWLSOUN)===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 10 June 1502 Magnus Paulson is noticed as the tacksman of the Bull of Halkisnes, an eighteen penny land on the Orkney island of Sanday. He also held a tack for the eighteen penny land of Gardymelis,  and the nine penny land 
2 CONC of Frow and Wattin, both also on the island of Sanday. [https://archive.org/stream/recordsofearldom00clou#page/419/mode/1up Records of the Earldom of Orkney, p. 419]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Magnus Paulson died before 17 March 1522-23, the date upon which his sons William Paulson and Henry Paulson sold their deceased mother's heritage rights in Orkney and Shetland to John Sinclair of Tollop. [https://archive.org/st
2 CONC ream/recordsofearldom00clou#page/205/mode/1up Records of the Earldon of Orkney, CII on pp. 205-06]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Magnus Paulson married Cristiane Sinclair. [https://archive.org/stream/recordsofearldom00clou#page/205/mode/1up Records of the Earldon of Orkney, charter number CII on pp. 205-06]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/William-Paulsoun/6000000049699005196?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1479057374295&through=6000000049699159161
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Henry-Paulsoun/6000000049699588946?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1479057568022&through=6000000049699159161
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the Rental of 1502-03===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 June 1502 [Made at Warsetter]: Parochia Sancti Crucis . . . . . Magnus Paulsoun, tacksman of the Bull of Halkisnes, 18d. land; Gardymelis, 18d. land; Frow and Wattin, 9d. land, and two towmales . . . . . [Records of the Earl
2 CONC dom of Orkney: 419]'''
