1 NAME John MacEwen /Cameron of Lochiel/ 18th Chief of Clan Cameron
2 GIVN John MacEwen
2 SURN Cameron of Lochiel
2 NSFX 18th Chief of Clan Cameron
2 _MARNM Cameron of Lochiel
2 NICK 18th Chief Cameron
2 NICK John Cameron XVIII Chief Cameron
2 NICK John Clan Chief CAMERON
2 NICK Donald John CAMERON Laird Lochiel
2 NICK John CAMERON
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1663
2 ADDR
3 CITY Lochiel, Lochaber
3 CTRY Scotland
1 OCCU Clan Chief
2 DATE 1719
1 DEAT
2 DATE 24 DEC 1748
2 ADDR
3 CITY Nieuport
3 STAE Comté de Flandre
3 CTRY France
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He died in 1747/48 at Nieuport, Belgium, in exile. He fought in the Battle of Sheriffmuir.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1715 he was a Jacobite, hence was attainted and his estates forfeited. He was created 1st Lord Lochiel [Jacobite] on 27 January 1717, by the titular King James VIII.
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the position of 18th Chief of Clan Cameron in 1719
2 CONT
2 CONT * Burke, Bernard, Sir.  [https://archive.org/stream/genealogicalhera01byuburk#page/252/mode/2up A genealogical and heraldic history of the landed gentry of Great Britain & Ireland 6th ed]. London : Harrison 1879. Vol I. page 253
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Cameron_of_Lochiel
2 CONT
2 CONT John Cameron of Lochiel (died 1748) was the 18th chief of Clan Cameron and a significant Jacobite. He was the eldest son and heir of Sir Ewen Cameron of Lochiel, a fervent Royalist and one of the first to join the rising of 1652 i
2 CONC n favour of King Charles II, by whom he was knighted in 1681.
2 CONT
2 CONT He joined the Earl of Mar in 1715 at the head of his Clan. On 27 January 1717, he was created by "King James VIII", otherwise known as the "Old Pretender" or "Old Chevalier", a Lord and Peer of Parliament in the Jacobite Peerage, 
2 CONC under the title of Lord Lochiel. He fought at the Battle of Glen Shiel in 1719, and died in exile in Flanders. http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Glen_Shiel
2 CONT
2 CONT His eldest son and successor was Donald Cameron of Lochiel, known as "Gentle Lochiel", who played an important role in the Jacobite Rising of 1745.
