1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT John Og MacKinnon married a daughter of MacDonald of Castleton. Tragically, he died at a very young age (around 1682)—reputedly on the very night his son, Iain Dubh, was born.
2 CONT
2 CONT Since John Og passed away before his own father, Sir Lachlan Mòr MacKinnon (the 28th Chief), he never actually held the title of Chief himself.Skipping a Generation: When Sir Lachlan Mòr died around 1700, the chiefship skipped wha
2 CONC t generation passing directly to the grandson, Iain Dubh, making him the 29th Chief.
