2 CONC  ID: I20259 Name: Hector Mor 12th Maclean , 8th Lord of Duart Sex: M Death: 1568 Event: Info 1 Lord of Dowart (Duart) & Morvaren. Hector Mor Eachann. Event: 1 Source See Burke's Peerage under "Maclean of Dowart" See also Stirnet G
2 CONC enealogy at http://www.stirnet.com/HTML/genie/british/mac/maclean02.htm Event: Info 5 See also "Clan MacLean/MacLaine Genealogy Database" at http://www.gillean.com/Roots/db.old/index.htm Note: The Clan Donald Genealogy Database at
2 CONC  http://www.clandonald.org.uk/genealogy.htm (This is a very large data base of Macdonald/Macdonell information, probably the most extensive on the web.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Hector (?) 1540 12th Chief, son of Lachlan Cattanach in 1540 captured by King James V. His daughter, Catherine was said to have been married to Archibald Roy Campbell and after his death to Calvagh O'Donnell and Shane O'Neill in I
2 CONC reland, on the latter's death in 1567 she returned to Mull. He was one of the principle supporters of Sir Donald Macdonald of Lochalsh, when, in November 1513, he brought forward his claims to the lordship of the Isles. In 1529 he
2 CONC  joined the Clan Donald of Isla against the Colin, 3rd Earl of Argyll, and ravaged with fire and sword the lands of Roseneath, Craignish, and others belonging to the Campbells, killing many of the inhabitants. The Campbells, on th
2 CONC eir part, retaliated by laying waste great portion of the isles of Mull and Tiree and the lands of Morvern, belonging to the Macleans. In May 1530, Mclean of Duart and Alexander of Isla made their personal submission to the sovere
2 CONC ign at Stirling, and, with the other rebel island chiefs who followed their example, were pardoned, upon giving security for their after obedience. In 1545, Maclean of Duart acted a very prominent part in the intrigues with Englan
2 CONC d, in furtherance of the project of Henry VIII, to force the Scottish nation to consent to a marriage between Prince Edward and the young Queen Mary. He and Maclean of Lochbuie were among the barons of the Isles who accompanied Do
2 CONC nald Dubh to Ireland, and at the command of the Earl of Lennox, claiming to be regent of Scotland, swore allegiance to the king of England.  http://www.fortunecity.com/bally/leitrim/147/maclean.html
2 CONT
2 CONT "12th chief, Hector Mor MacLean (Eachann) better known as Hector Mor, or Hector the Great in 1527, d in 1568 "Hector Mor married Mary, daughter of Alexander MacDonald of Islay and the Glens, by whom he had two sons and seven daugh
2 CONC ters, Eachann Og (successor), and John Dubh, predecessor or the family of Kinlochaline, Marian, Mary, Catherine, 2nd Catherine, Julian, Una & Janet. Argyle married Catherine, 2nd youngest daughter of Hector Mor (3rd wife) and Argy
2 CONC les daughter, Janet, married Hectors eldest son, Eachann Og (successor) During this time, a feud broke out between the MacLeans of Lochbuy and those of Duard, about the year 1537. John Og MacLean of Lochbuy and his two elder sons 
2 CONC were killed. The old feud between the Cameron's and MacLeans was renewed. In 1548, Donald Dubh, who had been in hopeless captivity for nearly 40 years, again managed to effect his escape. On his arrival to the Isles he was receive
2 CONC d with enthusiasm by the same clans which had supported him in 1506. He set out to expel the Earls of Argyle and Huntly for his long imprisonment. A HISTORY OF THE CLAN MACLEAN  "FROM ITS FIRST SETTLEMENT AT DUARD CASTLE, IN THE I
2 CONC SLE OF MULL, TO THE PRESENT PERIOD WRITTEN BY J.P. MACLEAN IN 1889
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Lachlan Catanach 11th Chief of Maclean b: 1465  Mother: Marian Maclean , of Treshnish
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 Mary MacDonald , of Islay and the Glens Children Has Children Hector (Eachann) Og 13th Chief Maclean Has Children Mary Maclean , of Duart Has Children daughter Maclean Has Children John Dubh Maclean , of Morvern Has Chi
2 CONC ldren Giles Julia\Jill Maclean , of Duart Has Children Janet Maclean , of Duart
2 CONT
