1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Janet Maclean is the daughter of Hector 'Mor' Maclean, 8th of Duart and Morven.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married 
2 CONT # Angus Macalister Macdonald, 7th of Glengarry, son of Alexander Macdonald, 6th of Glengarry and Margaret Macdonald
2 CONT # Allan MacDonald, 9th of Clanranald and Moidart
2 CONT # Archibald Campbell, 2nd of Lochnell (2nd wife)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT From Burke’s (1879), “CAMPBELL OF LOCHNELL.” Page 255.  < [https://archive.org/stream/genealogicalhera01byuburk#page/254/mode/2up Archive.Org] >
2 CONT
2 CONT >The eldest son, Archibald Campbell, 2nd of Lochnell, m. 1st, Janet, dau. of Duncan Macdougall, of Dunolly, and had, Alexander, his heir; and Colin, whose issue is extinct. He m. 2ndly, a dau. of Maclean of Dowart, and had issue ;
2 CONC  3rdly, a dau. of Cheyne, and had a son, John, ancestor of Coreleigh ; and 4tlhly,Sibella, dau. of John Drummond, of Colquhalzie, and had a son, James, of Cruachan, ancestor of Stonefield and Balemo.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT listed in Stirnet Campbell09 as daughter of Maclean of Dowart.
2 CONT
2 CONT Given name from LDS Medieval Families Unit, which confirms of Duart and provides parents but says she died sp.
