1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Catherine Maclean II, was married four times: firstly to Archibald Campbell, 4th Earl of Argyll; secondly to Calvagh O'Donnell, Lord of Tyrconnell[3]; thirdly to Shane O'Neill, Prince of Ulster; and fourthly to Joh
2 CONC n Stewart of Appin[4]. Catherine was a high-spirited woman, and was distinguished for her beauty and culture.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hector_Mor_Maclean,_12th_Chief
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT former wife of Calvagh O'Donnell
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1561 Calvagh [O'Donnell] and his wife were captured by Shane O'Neill in the monastery of Kildonnell. His wife, Catherine Maclean, who had previously been the wife of the Earl of Argyll, was kept by Shane O'Neill as his mistress
2 CONC  and bore him several children, though grossly ill-treated by her savage captor; Calvagh himself was subjected to atrocious torture during the three years that he remained O'Neill's prisoner.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.britannica.com/eb/article-9056771
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Name 	Catherine 'the elder' MacLean  [1]  Born 	Abt 1530  	Duart, Isle Of Mull, Argyll, Scotland  Gender 	Female  Name 	Katherine MacLean  [3]  Died 	Yes, date unknown 
2 CONT
2 CONT Father 	Hector Mor MacLean, 8th of Duart and of Morvern, 12th Chief,   b. 1497, Duart, Isle Of Mull, Argyll, Scotland ,   d. 1568  (Age 71 years) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother 	Mary MacDonald,   b. Abt 1497,   d. Yes, date unknown  Married 	Y  [1, 2, 4, 5, 6] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 1 	Archibald 'red' Campbell, 4th Earl of Argyll,   b. Aug 1502, Carrick, Argyllshire, Scotland,   d. 2 Dec 1558  (Age ~ 56 years)  Married 	Abt 1546  [3]  Marriage Contract 	12 Mar 1545-1546  	Doward, Herefordshire, England
2 CONC
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 2 	Calvagh O'Donnell, 3rd Lord of Tyrconnell,   b. Abt 1514, Tyrconnel, Donegal, Ireland,   d. 26 Nov 1566  (Age ~ 52 years)  Married 	Abt 1559  	Argyllshire, Scotland 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children  	
2 CONT
2 CONT +	1. Conn O'Donnell,   d. Yes, date unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 3 	John Stewart, 4th of Appin,   b. Abt 1514, Appin, Argyllshire, Scotland ,   d. Abt 1595  (Age ~ 81 years)  Married 	Bef 6 Apr 1575  	Doward, Herefordshire, England
2 CONT --------------------
