2 CONT https://landedfamilies.blogspot.com/2013/04/23-adair-of-ballymena-castle-and.html?m=1
2 CONT
2 CONT Ninian Adair (d. c.1606) of Kinhilt.  Elder son of Sir William Adair (d. 1593) and his wife Lady Helen, daughter of Gilbert Kennedy, 2nd Earl of Cassillis; probably born about 1545. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married 18 June 1566 Elizabeth, daughter of Sir James Gordon of Kirkpatrick (and Lochinvar?) and widow of John Grierson (d. 1558) of Lag, and had issue including:
2 CONT * (1) William Adair (d. 1626) (q.v.); 
2 CONT * (2) Patrick Adair (fl. 1614);
2 CONT * (2) James Adair of Maryport;
2 CONT * (4) Rt. Rev. Archibald Adair (d. 1646), Dean of Rapho (1616), Bishop of Killaloe 1639-40 (deprived) and Bishop of Waterford & Lismore, 1641-46;
2 CONT * (5) Gilbert Adair (b. c.1582?; fl. 1610);
2 CONT * (6) Thomas Adair (d. before 1610), provost of Stranraer.
2 CONT
2 CONT He inherited the Kinhilt estate, and the castles of St. John and Dunskey from his father in 1593. He died in about 1608.
