2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 December 1610: Charter by James Earl of Glencairn to William Master of Glencairn, his eldest son ("senior son and apparent heir") and Dame Jamet Ker his wife in liferent and the heirs male (procreated or) to be procreate betw
2 CONC een them, whom failing to the nearest lawful (heir) male of the Master of Glencairn mentioned in the new entail of the lordship and Earldom of Glencairn, of the lands and barony of Glencairn with the castle etc. lying in the count
2 CONC y of Dumfries and lands and barony of Kilmaurs lying in the county of Ayr the Charter granted in implement of a contract entered into between the Earl on the one part and William Master of Glencairn and Dame Janet Ker his wife, da
2 CONC ughter of the deceased Mark Earl of Lothian (on the 2nd part) and Dame Margaret Maxwell Countess of Lothian mother of the said Dame Janet Ker on the third part dated 24th November 1610, but with and under the reservations provisio
2 CONC ns and conditions mentioned in the said contract. (This only refers to the barony of Kilmaurs). Witnesses, Sir James Cunningham of Glengarnock, knight, William Barclay of Innergelly, George and James Cunninghams burgesses of Edinb
2 CONC urgh (Geo. C. burgess of Canongate, John C., merchant burgess of Edinburgh). Robert Fergusson, apparent of Craigdarroch, one of the baillies for the Earl of Glencairn. At Canongate. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlineca
2 CONC talogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f1%2f156&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=craigdarroch&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1620&di=n National Records of Scotland, Earls of Glencairn, reference GD39/1/156]'''
