1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lachlan_Maclean,_3rd_Laird_of_Torloisk
2 CONT
2 CONT Lachlan Maclean, 3rd Laird of Torloisk was a 17th-century Scottish nobleman. He managed the estate of Sir John Maclean, 4th Baronet with Lauchlan Maclean, 2nd Laird of Brolas during his minority.[1]
2 CONT He was reputed one of the most gallant and accomplished gentlemen of his time, and well qualified for the highest station in the gift of his country. He did not aspire to state intrigue, but contented himself in looking after affa
2 CONC irs of interest to his clan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lachlan Maclean, 3rd Laird of Torloisk, married Barbara, daughter of Alexander MacDonald of Sleat, brother of Sir James Mor Macdonald, 9th Laird of Sleat, and had issue, two sons and one daughter:
2 CONT
2 CONT *Hector Maclean of Torloisk, who died at the age of eighteen
2 CONT *Alexander Maclean, 4th Laird of Torloisk (1690-1715), was captain in the Second battalion of the Scots Guards, and served in the Spanish wars; at age twenty-five, he had his leg broken at the Battle of Brihuega, in Spain, in 1710
2 CONC , by a musket ball, of which he fevered and died; dying without children, he was succeeded by his cousin
2 CONT *Jannet Maclean of Torloisk, married to Archibald Campbell of Inverawe.
2 CONT
2 CONT It was in 1685 that Lachlan besieged, captured, and destroyed the castle of Carnassary, and, as is shown by the petition of Duncan Campbell. He died prior to 1690.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT *An Historical and Genealogical Account of the Clan Maclean: From Its First ... By Lachlan MacLean.  Page 350.  [https://books.google.com/books?id=bBJbAAAAYAAJ&lpg=PA350&ots=JrFAKZeYdt&dq=Barbara%20Macdonald%20hector%20maclean&pg=
2 CONC PA350#v=onepage&q=Barbara%20Macdonald%20hector%20maclean&f=true GoogleBooks]
2 CONT *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laird_of_Torloisk “The Laird of Torloisk was the hereditary owner of an estate on the Isle of Mull”
2 CONT *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isle_of_Mull
