1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sir_Allan_Maclean,_6th_Baronet
2 CONT
2 CONT == Wikipedia Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir Allan Maclean, 6th Baronet of Morvern</strong> (1710 – 10 December 1783) was the 22nd Clan Chief of Clan Maclean from 1750 till his death in 1783. He was the 4th Laird of Brolas. He died without leaving an heir to his
2 CONC  title and the title was bestowed on his closest living male relative, a fourth cousin, [http://www.geni.com/people/Sir-Hector-Maclean-7th-Baronet/6000000018719645899 Sir Hector Maclean, 7th Baronet].
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in 1710 in Torloisk to Donald Maclean, 3rd Laird of Brolas. He became the Clan Maclean Chief when [http://www.geni.com/people/Hector-Maclean/6000000018499276287 Sir Hector Maclean, 5th Baronet], his third cousin, died 
2 CONC without an heir in 1750...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...He married Anne, daughter of Hector Maclean of Coll and had the following daughters:
2 CONT * Maria Maclean, married Charles Maclean of Kinlochaline
2 CONT * Sibella Maclean, married John Maclean of Inverscadell
2 CONT * Ann Maclean, married Dr. Mackenzie Grieve of Edinburgh
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife died in 1760."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: Wikipedia contributors, 'Sir Allan Maclean, 6th Baronet', <em>Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia</em>, 19 November 2012, 00:52 UTC, <http://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Sir_Allan_Maclean,_6th_Baronet&oldid=523764949> 
2 CONC [accessed 19 December 2012]
